# Names the deployed code reads, absent from docker-compose.yml on purpose, whose
# default `code-drift.sh` cannot see (kolonie-infra#90).
#
# **This file is the short residue and not a suppression list.** The check's own
# rule catches a default written beside the read — `process.env[X] ?? 60_000`.
# What it cannot catch is a default applied by the *callee*, and that is the only
# thing that belongs here.
#
# One name per line, then the reason. A name here is reported as deliberate and
# does not fail the run, so a line without a reason is a line somebody should
# have argued for instead of adding.
#
# Adding a name here to silence a real finding is the failure mode. The two
# defects #90 exists to catch — SMS_COLONY_NUMBER and MASTODON_VERIFIER_INSTANCES
# — are both fixed in docker-compose.yml, not listed here, and neither belongs
# here ever.

DIRECTION_MODEL  the default is applied inside openRouterDirectionClassifier(), not at the call site — kolonie-platform's packages/verifiers holds DEFAULT_DIRECTION_MODEL beside it. Documented there as "Overridable, because the choice will be revisited".
